background #8a6444
; The Hall of Vanes: the round ground floor of the Spire, lamplit. The
; back wall curves away; the hearth on the left, the weathervanes on the
; wall, the speaking-tube and the stair behind its wind-gate on the right;
; evening light from a west window lies across the boards. Then, in
; layers: the bellows on their hook (and the ribbon that mends them), the
; wind-gate shut and open, Ysolde, and the armchair in front of her.
